<pageinfo><controlpgno entity="n3839003">003</controlpgno><printpgno></printpgno></pageinfo>
<div type="idinfo">
<p>
<hi rend="other">
In Memoriam
<lb>
Grace Raymond Hebard
<lb>
1861-1936
</hi>
</p>
<p>
<hi rend="other">
Published by
<lb>
The Faculty of the University of Wyoming
<lb>
June, 1937
</hi>
</p>
</div>
<pageinfo><controlpgno entity="n3839004">004</controlpgno><printpgno></printpgno></pageinfo>
<div>
<p>
<handwritten>
JA93
<lb>
.H4I5
</handwritten>
</p>
<p>
<hi rend="other">
Grace Raymond Hebard,
</hi>
<lb>
engineer, administrator,librarian, historian, champion of womanhood, citizen, teacher, and friend of youth.  A library of her books preserve for us the heroic history of our pioneer; women enjoy more quality; a University lives more richly; a multitude of youth of yesterday and today honor the memory of her friendliness; future students will enjoy her benefactions; and all these because she lived and served.  We mourn her absence but we glory in her record of noble achievement.
</p>
<p>
<hi rend="smallcaps">
Arthur Griswold Crane.
</hi>
</p>
<p>
<stamped>
LIBRARY OF CONGRESS
<lb>
OCT 5 1937
<lb>
DIVISION OF DOCUMENTS
</stamped>
</p>
</div>
<pageinfo><controlpgno entity="n3839005">005</controlpgno><printpgno>3</printpgno></pageinfo>
<div>
<head>
Chronology
</head>
<list>
<item>
<p>
1861
<hsep>
Grace Raymond Hebard born July 2, in Clinton, Iowa.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1882
<hsep>
Bachelor of Science degree, University of Iowa.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1882
<hsep>
Came to Wyoming as draftsman in Surveyor General&apos;s office Cheyenne.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1885
<hsep>
Master of Arts, degree, University of Iowa.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1889
<hsep>
Championed woman suffrage clause before Wyoming State Constitutional Convention.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1891
<hsep>
Appointed Deputy State Engineer under Dr. Elwood Mead.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1891
<hsep>
Appointed by Governor Amos Barber as member and secretary of University Board of Trustee.  Served as board member of the library committee.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1993
<hsep>
Doctor of Philosophy degree from Illinois Wesleyan University
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1898
<hsep>
Admitted to the Wyoming bar.
</p>
</item>
<item>
<p>
1904
<hsep>
